1. What is a DaemonSet?
A DaemonSet ensures that a copy of a particular Pod runs on each eligible Kubernetes node.
2. Create daemonset.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: DaemonSet

metadata:
  name: nginx-daemonset

spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx-daemon

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx-daemon

    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx-container
          image: nginx:latest
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80
4. Check DaemonSet
kubectl get daemonsets
kubectl get ds
5. Check DaemonSet details
kubectl describe daemonset nginx-daemonset
